diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 764902bce..eff87c953 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -102,6 +102,7 @@ Some features are not supported in AdvCiv-SAS; e.g., non-English languages, pre-
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5429+) **Launch guard for SAS defines (startup/load/Sevopedia):** Added a strict define-integrity check using one **int sentinel** and one **string sentinel**, validated at pre-game start, game start, save load, Sevopedia creation, and Sevopedia show. If a value is missing or mismatched, Python raises a **fatal error** with `actual` vs `expected` values and guidance to launch from a Windows shortcut. The game will be **unplayable if the config is incorrect**. Change in: [`SASDefineGuard.py`](/Assets/Python/SASDefineGuard.py). See also [Quick Install Guide](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Quick_Install_Setup_Guide.md#place-a-shortcut-of-the-mod-on-your-desktop).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5442+) **Fail-fast XML lookup hardening:** replaced `getInfoTypeForString(...)` calls (terrain/features/bonuses and similar tags) with `getInfoTypeOrFail(...)` (in [SASUtils.py](/Assets/Python/SASUtils.py)), so **missing/renamed XML tags raise explicit errors** instead of silently using invalid `-1` values.
 - **Heavily refactor and simplify Sevopedia Main** so it is much easier to add, reorder, or modify or otherwise maintain categories. See [Sevopedia reworks (example 0.0)](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Sevopedia_Reworks.md#example-00-heavily-refactored-sevopedia-maintain-so-it-is-much-easier-to-maintain-or-customize).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5452+) Convert **single quote to double quote** (e.g. `'BONUS_IRON'` to `"BONUS_IRON"`), which allowed to **detect and fix incorrect fields** and later strengthen them with `getInfoTypeOrFail(...)`.
 - **Performance & code cleanup:** Broad Python/XML/C++ optimizations (e.g., removed giant ConfigObj docstring (see [KI#21.5](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#215---addressed--fixed---removed-the-giant-configobj-docstring-very-inefficiently-in-the-python-code-and-commented-out-most-if-not-all-as-well)); cached hot values via `static const`/hoisting; normalized inconsistent asset names (see for example [KI#18](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#18---very-inconsistent-naming-in-some-assets))), **map-type heaviness caching** (`CvGame::recomputeMapnameHeaviness`) so land/naval checks run once per game (feeds UNITAI tuning) (see [KI#42](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#42---enhancedaddressed-tune-ais-preferred-based-unitai-based-on-war-status-offense-mode-defense-mode-combined-power-ratios-of-ennemies-etc-if-any-other-general-sanity-checks-and-efficiency-city-size-map-type-land-heavy-vs-water-heavy-vs-other-if-any-for-example-general-suicide-or-such-tendencies-etc), **bonus-specific builds/improvements caching** (e.g. `CvUnitAI::getBonusSpecificLandBuilds`), [AI Personality Panel performance optimization notes](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_AI_Personality_Panel.md#notes-about-performance-optimization-of-the-ai-personality-panel-caching)), **feature-level caching** (AI Personality Panel), refactor **extremely redundant code** (e.g. `refreshUnitSelection` in [CvMilitaryAdvisor.py](/Assets/Python/Screens/CvMilitaryAdvisor.py)), cache redundant computation (e.g. **store per turn and player** top cities' values `CvCityAI::AI_buildingValue`), etc.
 - **Found-value** evaluation now uses **`int`** end-to-end (CitySiteEvaluator, AIFoundValue, CvPlot cache, SPI, Python callback), **not `short`**. Why: **avoid overflow/underflow** and short wraparounds in site scoring; keep the logic the same while **improving reliability**. Expectation: more robust site values, fewer edge-case penalties/boosts from short overflow; no known negative gameplay change. Performance: `int` is typically at least as fast as short on modern CPUs; no slowdown expected. Tested: autoplay ran fine. See [Change from short to int the Found value pipeline](/README.md#change-from-short-to-int-the-found-value-pipeline).
 - Removed the old clunky Base AdvCiv's `CONCEPT_TRAIT` XML clutter. Now using the more efficient `WIDGET_PYTHON` similarly instead.
@@ -352,11 +353,11 @@ Note: New panels added or modified mostly not mentioned here for concision. See
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5433+) **Earth2 start distribution rework:** for Huge and beyond world sizes, keep Earth2 at its existing **Huge-scale sizing** (already large enough), but solve crowding by **populating underused landmasses instead** (e.g., min 16 players before Africa is populated, min 32 players before the whole world is populated) of enlarging the script further. **Thresholds are based on player count** (not world size). See [`GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml`](/Assets/XML/GlobalDefines_advciv_sas.xml).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5444+) Add **Deer percentage map option** (e.g., `0/10/25/50/75/100`) for [Arboria.py](/PrivateMaps/Arboria.py) and [Boreal.py](/PrivateMaps/Boreal.py): **high-food terrain** (e.g. grass) maps like Arboria, or **lower-food terrain** ones (e.g. tundra/plains) like Boreal, had **too much deer**. See also See [KI#105](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#105---fixed-base-advciv-bug-of-most-bonuses-eg-deer-sometimes-not-appearing-at-first-civ4-launch-in-some-maps-eg-boreal).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5446+) **Order maps alphabetically** in **Simple Game** or **Custom Game** (by adding missing map scripts in **PrivateMaps**).
-- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5439+) **Remove from Simple Game** some maps that are deemed not essential or unbalanced; they are remain playable via the **Custom Game** menu: [Shuffle.py](/PrivateMaps/Shuffle.py), [Tectonics.py](/PrivateMaps/Tectonics.py), [Hemispheres.py](/PrivateMaps/Hemispheres.py), [Big_and_Small.py](/PrivateMaps/Big_and_Small.py), [Great_Plains.py](/PrivateMaps/Great_Plains.py), [Oasis.py](/PrivateMaps/Oasis.py).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5439+) **Remove from Simple Game** some maps that are deemed not essential or unbalanced; they are remain playable via the **Custom Game** menu: [Big_and_Small.py](/PrivateMaps/Big_and_Small.py), [Great_Plains.py](/PrivateMaps/Great_Plains.py), [Earth2.py](/PrivateMaps/Earth2.py), [Hemispheres.py](/PrivateMaps/Hemispheres.py), [Lakes.py](/PrivateMaps/Lakes.py) (has too few lakes), [Oasis.py](/PrivateMaps/Oasis.py), [Shuffle.py](/PrivateMaps/Shuffle.py), [Tectonics.py](/PrivateMaps/Tectonics.py).
